Search, library browsing, and playlists are all local — nothing leaves the
device. Identification, tagging, and read behavior are all tunable from
settings.

![Music Player settings page](/projects/music-player/settings.png)

A lot of libraries are untagged or mistagged, so identification leans on the
filename as much as the tags. Artists, a title, and noise like "(Lyrics)" or
a trailing download id all get parsed out first:

```ts
function parseFilename(path: string): ParsedName {
	let base = (path.split('/').pop() ?? path).replace(/\.[^.]+$/, '');
	base = stripNoise(base);
	if (!/\s/.test(base)) base = base.replace(/_+/g, ' ').trim();
	base = base.replace(/^\d{1,3}\s*[-.)]\s+/, ''); // "01 - "
	const sep = base.split(/\s+[-–—]\s+/);
	if (sep.length < 2) return { artists: [], title: stripFeat(base).title || base };
	const artistPart = sep[0];
	let title = sep.slice(1).join(' - ').replace(/^\(\d+\)\s*/, '');
	const featured = stripFeat(title);
	title = featured.title;
	return { artists: [...splitArtists(artistPart), ...featured.artists], title };
}
```

That parsed name goes out as a MusicBrainz query, and candidates come back
scored against title, artist, duration and MusicBrainz's own confidence —
weighted differently depending on whether the filename actually named an
artist:

```ts
const confidence = hasArtist
	? 0.35 * t + 0.3 * a + 0.25 * d + 0.1 * mb
	: 0.5 * t + 0.4 * d + 0.1 * mb;
```

A match only auto-applies above a confidence threshold, with the file's
duration agreeing within a few seconds — anything shakier gets left for
"Choose match" instead of guessed at:

```ts
export function isConfident<T extends Scorable>(
	ranked: Ranked<T>[],
	rule: ConfidenceRule = { threshold: CONFIDENT, applyOnTies: false, requireStudio: false, durationSec: null }
): boolean {
	const [best, ...rest] = ranked;
	if (!best || best.confidence < rule.threshold) return false;
	if (!rule.durationSec || !best.lengthMs) return false;
	if (Math.abs(best.lengthMs / 1000 - rule.durationSec) > DURATION_TOLERANCE_SEC) return false;
	if (rule.requireStudio && !best.releases?.some(isStudioType)) return false;
	if (rule.applyOnTies) return true;
	const rival = rest.find((r) => !sameSong(best, r));
	return !rival || best.confidence - rival.confidence >= MARGIN;
}
```
